      <section id="FamilyBudgetDecisionLimitations" class="content-section">
        <h2>What these calculators can and cannot answer</h2>

        <p>
          These calculators can organize the money side of baby and parenting decisions.
          They cannot decide whether to have a child, when your family is emotionally
          ready, what medical advice applies to your situation, or which childcare
          arrangement is best. Use the result as a pressure test, then combine it with
          benefits information, insurance details, medical guidance, childcare availability,
          and your own family priorities.
        </p>

        <div class="family-hub-callout">
          <p>
            The safest family budget is not the one with the lowest baby cost estimate.
            It is the one that keeps monthly breathing room, protects emergency savings,
            counts debt honestly, and still has a fallback plan when timing gets messy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

